          "title": "You'll want to know: کسکنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کسکنا — kasaknā — \"to ache dully; to twinge\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سردی میں پرانا زخم کسکتا ہے۔ sardī meṅ purānā zakhm kasaktā hai. The old wound aches in the cold."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): وہ زخم رات بھر کسکا, voh zakhm rāt bhar kaskā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کسکنا (kasaknā) is inherited: CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin kasaknā, \"to ache\", under Sanskrit kaṣati, \"scratches\", which an old list of roots also gives as \"hurts\" (CDIAL 2972)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
